{number: 128}
{title: Are You Washed in the Blood?}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Have you been to Jesus for the cleansing pow'r?
Are you washed in the [F] blood of the [C] Lamb?
Are you fully trusting in His grace this hour?
Are you washed in the [G7] blood of the [C] Lamb?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Are you [C] washed in the blood,
In the [F] soul-cleansing blood of the [C] Lamb?
Are your garments spotless? Are they white as snow?
Are you washed in the [G7] blood of the [C] Lamb?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Are you [C] walking daily by the Savior's side?
Are you washed in the [F] blood of the [C] Lamb?
Do you rest each moment in the Crucified?
Are you washed in the [G7] blood of the [C] Lamb?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
When the [C] Bridegroom cometh will your robes be white?
Are you washed in the [F] blood of the [C] Lamb?
Will your soul be ready for the mansions bright,
And be washed in the [G7] blood of the [C] Lamb?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Lay a-[C] side the garments that are stained with sin,
And be washed in the [F] blood of the [C] Lamb;
There's a fountain flowing for the soul unclean,
O be washed in the [G7] blood of the [C] Lamb!
{end_of_verse}
